    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into September 13 with a lineup anchored by the high-upside production of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.44) and **Jackson Merrill** (67.81). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against the lefty Rogers, pushing his score toward the top of our ledger, while **Jackson Merrill** is a prime start due to a projected wind-out condition providing a +10% boost to his output despite facing a tough arm in Webb. **Kyle Tucker** (64.80) and **Sam Antonacci** (64.60) also offer elite stability; **Sam Antonacci** remains a critical piece for our category-wide stolen base hunt, leveraging his leadoff spot and a soft matchup against McGreevy to maintain a high-floor scoring profile.\n\nPlatoon advantages are driving significant value today, particularly for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.29) and **Gunnar Henderson** (60.92). While **Gunnar Henderson** faces the difficult Cease, his dynamic platoon edge (+14%) keeps him well within the \"Strong\" start tier. Conversely, **Coby Mayo** (38.12) is the most notable exclusion from today\u2019s lineup. Although he holds promise, his poor efficiency rating against the elite stuff of Cease coupled with a negative platoon variance kept him beneath our strict 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" We are currently navigating a depleted bench with **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, leaving little room for error if weather-related risks emerge for our starters. Given the scarcity of stolen bases, we are prioritizing the speed-oriented profiles of **Sam Antonacci** and the rest of the daily starters to maximize our 5x5 potential as we head into the final weeks of the season.",
